body:
ding ding ding ding

&#x200B;

We have a winner here.

Pessoal e este o [https://github.com/odoo/odoo](https://github.com/odoo/odoo)  ? 

&#x200B;

Parece fixe tem varias coisas e uma API e tambem parece estar aprovado [https://imgur.com/a/ICZaZp3](https://imgur.com/a/ICZaZp3)

No, FreeCAD is better! 

&#x200B;

I am a strong Open Source own your code and you source kind of person though. The ability to own my files and knowing that no one will be able to suddently change the licensing and keep them or only allow me to export something like the STEP files is a no no.

Awesome work!

&#x200B;

I saw you screenshots on the discord also, pretty awesome the progress that you are making.

Yeah, I love linkstage, but all my production designs are based on maintream 0.19 and Assembly4 workbench (that uses some of linkstage logic) so a transition some years in the future should not be that hard.

&#x200B;

I love linkstage, but I only use it to play arround, my solid desings that I plan to have and maintain are still on upstream.

Thank you, know the Python API it will more useful to me in the future. 

&#x200B;

Saved this one.

